implementationPlan.description:
THE FIX — one condition, one file. In apps/daemon/src/repository/git-publication-credentials.ts export the measured sentinel and admit it:
  /** Git refuses to url-match a remote with no `://` scheme (scp-style SSH, a local bare repository). LC_ALL=C is pinned by landingEnvironment(), so this line is stable; an unrecognised stderr still fails closed. */
  export const UNMATCHABLE_REMOTE_FATAL = "fatal: invalid URL scheme name or missing '://' suffix";
and insert, immediately after the existing line-7 arm and BEFORE the `result.code !== 0` throw:
  if (result.code === 128 && result.stdout === "" && result.stderr.split(/\r?\n/u).some((line) => line === UNMATCHABLE_REMOTE_FATAL)) return [];
Strict equality per line — not `stderr.includes`, not a trimmed whole-buffer compare, not `code !== 0`. Change NOTHING else: the three-key allowlist (credential.helper / credential.usehttppath / credential.username), the /[\r\n\0]/u value injection guard, the missing-separator throw and the `--get-urlmatch` argv all stay byte-identical. Do not touch admitRemoteUrl, do not add an option to GitPublicationOptions. Re-run the step-1 leg: all four arms GREEN.
